    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start for the tone. But it feels a bit one-sided, like he's just shouting at clouds. To make him a real threat in the book, his arguments need to be harder to dismiss. Can you rewrite it so he's not just complaining about \"corporations,\" but actually making a specific, logical case for why the technocratic model is fundamentally incompatible with human freedom and democracy? Like, give him some actual points that would make a regular person stop and think \"maybe he's right.\"",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
